---
import LessonShell from '../../layouts/LessonShell.astro';

const installSnippet = `cargo install lolrust
lolrust path/to/your.meow --run`;
---
<LessonShell
    course="LolRust"
    number={16}
    name="Final Project ~ FizzBuzz"
    objective="Combine everything you learned. Print numbers 1-100, but for multiples of 3 print 'Fizz', for 5 print 'Buzz', for both print 'FizzBuzz'."
    keywords={[
        { code: 'chase n around 1..=100', note: 'iterate a range (for n in 1..=100)' },
        { code: 'if ceiling cat sez', note: 'classic if (also: when works)' },
        { code: 'or if ceiling cat sez', note: 'else if' },
        { code: 'or basement cat sez', note: 'else (the dark alternative)' },
        { code: 'n % 5', note: 'modulo ~ remainder when dividing' },
    ]}
    initial={`iz main() {
    // Loop from 1 to 100 (inclusive)
    chase n around 1..=100 {

        // FizzBuzz: divisible by both 3 AND 5 (so 15)
        if ceiling cat sez n % 15 == 0 {
            meow!("FizzBuzz");
        }
        // Fizz: divisible by 3
        or if ceiling cat sez n % 3 == 0 {
            meow!("Fizz");
        }

        // TODO 1: add a Buzz case for multiples of 5
        // hint: the pattern is exactly like Fizz above

        // TODO 2: add an else case that prints just the number
        // hint: use 'or basement cat sez' and meow!("{}", n)

    }
}`}
    checks={[
        { label: 'has for n in 1..=100', pattern: '\\bfor\\s+n\\s+in\\s+1\\.\\.=100\\b' },
        { label: 'prints FizzBuzz', pattern: '"FizzBuzz"' },
        { label: 'prints Fizz', pattern: '"Fizz"' },
        { label: 'prints Buzz (you added this)', pattern: '"Buzz"' },
        { label: 'checks % 5 (Buzz case)', pattern: '%\\s*5\\s*==' },
        { label: 'has else case', pattern: '\\belse\\b' },
        { label: 'prints the number itself', pattern: 'println!\\s*\\(\\s*"\\{\\}",\\s*n' },
        { label: 'no leftover lolrust keywords', pattern: '\\b(iz|chase|around|ceiling cat sez|basement cat sez|meow!)\\b', negate: true },
    ]}
    prev={{ href: '/lolrust/lesson-15', label: 'lesson 15' }}
    award="🐱 Master of LolRust 🐱"
>
    <div slot="extras" class="capstone-extras">
        <h3>This is your capstone</h3>
        <p class="dim">
            No new keywords ~ this is the test of whether you can <em>combine</em>
            what you've learned. You're filling in two TODOs to complete a
            classic FizzBuzz. The No Touchie Checker grades structurally ~
            it verifies your code prints all four cases (FizzBuzz, Fizz,
            Buzz, plain numbers) and uses the right control flow.
        </p>
        <p class="dim">
            Get all checks green to earn the <strong style="color: var(--yellow);">🏆 Golden Loaf</strong>.
        </p>

        <h3>What's next?</h3>
        <p class="dim">
            Meowademy runs the transpiler in your browser, but it can't
            actually <em>execute</em> your Rust ~ for that you need rustc.
            Install lolrust locally to write programs that take input,
            read files, and run for real:
        </p>
        <pre class="mono install-snippet">{installSnippet}</pre>
        <p class="dim">
            Then graduate to the example programs ~ the
            <a href="https://github.com/AdaInTheLab/lolrust/blob/main/examples/guessing_game.meow">guessing game</a>
            uses everything you learned plus stdin.
        </p>
    </div>
</LessonShell>

<style>
    .install-snippet {
        background: var(--bg-deep);
        border: 2px solid var(--yellow);
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        padding: 14px;
    }
</style>
